OneiOS 5002: the AIR Metal library (Jesvi-iOS's libredwoodair, its tools/mesa/air-metal.patch and
air-panfrost.patch) as libOneiOSRadeonAir, the library OneiOSRadeonMetal.bundle loads, and
air_metal_test, its host test on softpipe.

Jesvi declared both in freedreno's and panfrost's meson files, because they need libgallium and
a driver. Here they are a target of their own, src/gallium/targets/air-metal, read after every
driver, so that the A56's radeonsi build and a softpipe-only host build read the same file.

Two options (meson.options):
  -Doneios-air=true            build them; and count as a graphics and compute build
                               (with_gfx_compute): without OpenGL or Vulkan Mesa otherwise builds
                               NIR as headers only and libgallium without its compilers, and the
                               AIR library needs both (radeonsi's gfx part needs it as well)
  -Doneios-air-screen=radeonsi the library opens the A56's screen with
                               oneios_radeonsi_screen_create (the guest Mesa stage's; contract K3);
                               =none (the default) opens no GPU: only RWA_SOFTWARE=1 softpipe
userland/metal-amd/air/build.sh sets both.

diff --git a/meson.build b/meson.build
